<title>HONG KONG: Philippine Air FRN raised to US$200 mln.</title>
<headline>Philippine Air FRN raised to US$200 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine Airlines Inc's three-year floating rate note issue has been increased to US$200 million from US$100 million due to oversubscription, said arranger AB Capital Markets (HK).</p>
<p>The notes were launched on December 4 and priced at par to float at 200 basis points over the six-month London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>With fees, the all-in return for top-tier managers is 225 basis points.</p>
<p>The other arranger is Deutsche Morgan Grenfell Singapore.</p>
<p>AB Capital Markets (HK) said 34 institutions joined in the syndication.</p>
<p>The payment date was January 16.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6960</p>
</text>
